    "result_text": "Done. All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`), including the new `AcceptanceTest` that asserts `telephone` stays `+61412345678` while `telephoneDisplay` is `+61 412 345 678`.\n\nWhat I changed:\n\n- **`E164Telephone.countryCode(...)`** \u2014 a small package-private method exposing the recognised-country-code knowledge that already lived (privately) in this class, so nothing duplicates the country-code table. It splits an E.164 value's leading digits against the known codes.\n\n- **`TelephoneDisplay`** (new) \u2014 a single-responsibility, pure lookup helper parallel to `AgeBand`/`Locality`. Given the stored E.164 string it emits `country code + space + national digits grouped in threes`, delegating the country-code split to `E164Telephone`. Null/blank in \u2192 null out; unrecognised code \u2192 whole number grouped without a split.\n\n- **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 one `@Mapping` plus a `telephoneDisplay(owner)` default that calls `TelephoneDisplay.of(owner.getTelephone())`, matching the existing derived-field pattern. The raw `telephone` mapping is untouched.\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema (a derived field, so it sits alongside `displayName`/`initials`, not in `OwnerFields`), which drives the generated DTO.\n\nThe E.164 normalization and the raw `telephone` field are unchanged; the display value is computed purely on read.",
